/**
 * RustBridge - Kotlin → Rust FFI bridge via uniffi
 * 
 * This class wraps uniffi-generated bindings to provide a clean Kotlin API
 * for calling Rust functions from the mobile app.
 * 
 * Data Flow:
 *   1. HealthConnectManager reads data from Health Connect
 *   2. HealthSyncWorker batches data
 *   3. RustBridge converts to uniffi types
 *   4. Rust core processes (HRV calculation, pattern detection, storage)
 *   5. Results returned to Kotlin
 * 
 * Implementation Notes:
 *   - This is a STUB implementation for design purposes
 *   - Actual uniffi bindings generated at build time from Rust lib.rs
 *   - uniffi translates Kotlin types to Rust types automatically
 *   - See HeXuS/rust-core/lib.rs for Rust FFI interface definition
 * 
 * Build Process:
 *   1. cargo build --target aarch64-linux-android --release
 *   2. uniffi-bindgen generate src/lib.rs --language kotlin --out-dir ../mobile/android/uniffi
 *   3. Copy libhexus_core.so to mobile/android/app/src/main/jniLibs/arm64-v8a/
 *   4. Import generated bindings: import uniffi.hexus_core.*
 */
object RustBridge {

